# 📘 Verb Rules (SSC CGL के लिए महत्वपूर्ण)

## 🔹 Rule 1: Subject और Verb में Number (Singular/Plural) का मेल होना चाहिए।

👉 Singular Subject → Singular Verb
👉 Plural Subject → Plural Verb

✔ Example:

* He **plays** cricket. ✅
* They **play** cricket. ✅

❌ Wrong: He **play** cricket.

---

## 🔹 Rule 2: Collective Noun

अगर Collective Noun (team, jury, family, class) को एक unit की तरह लिया जाए तो Singular Verb लगेगी, लेकिन अगर individuals पर जोर हो तो Plural Verb लगेगी।

✔ Example:

* The team **is** playing well. (एक unit के रूप में)
* The team **are** fighting among themselves. (व्यक्तियों के रूप में)

---

## 🔹 Rule 3: Either…or / Neither…nor

Verb हमेशा **nearest subject** के अनुसार लगेगी।

✔ Example:

* Either Ram or his friends **are** coming.
* Neither the students nor the teacher **is** present.

---

## 🔹 Rule 4: With, Along with, Together with, As well as, In addition to

Verb हमेशा **पहले Subject** के अनुसार लगेगी।

✔ Example:

* Ram, along with his friends, **is** coming.
* The teacher, as well as the students, **is** present.

---

## 🔹 Rule 5: Singular Indefinite Pronouns (Each, Everyone, Someone, No one, Anybody, Everybody, Neither, Either) → हमेशा Singular Verb लेंगे।

✔ Example:

* Each boy **was** present.
* Everyone **knows** the answer.

---

## 🔹 Rule 6: Plural Indefinite Pronouns (Few, Many, Several, Both) → Plural Verb लेंगे।

✔ Example:

* Both boys **are** intelligent.
* Many students **have** passed.

---

## 🔹 Rule 7: Distance, Time, Money → Singular माना जाता है।

✔ Example:

* Ten kilometers **is** a long distance.
* Fifty rupees **is** a big amount.
* Two hours **is** enough.

---

## 🔹 Rule 8: Words ending with -s (news, mathematics, physics, politics, measles, economics) → Singular माने जाते हैं।

✔ Example:

* Mathematics **is** an interesting subject.
* Politics **is** a dirty game.

---

## 🔹 Rule 9: “A number of” और “The number of”

* **A number of** → Plural Verb
* **The number of** → Singular Verb

✔ Example:

* A number of students **are** absent.
* The number of students **is** small.

---

## 🔹 Rule 10: None

* जब ‘none’ का मतलब *not one* हो → Singular Verb
* जब *not any* हो → Plural Verb

✔ Example:

* None of the work **is** done.
* None of the boys **are** present.

---

